Feature: Views
  C selects the next of three views: [[line of sight]] from the pilot box, [[chase]] from
  behind the plane, and [[FPV]] through its nose camera. The CAM line on the HUD shows the
  view. In line of sight, auto-zoom keeps the plane at a good size on the screen when it
  flies away. Z turns auto-zoom off and on.

  Expectation: Chase follows the plane
    The view moves behind the plane and follows it. You see the area in front of the plane,
    and you also see the plane.
    Given the view is line of sight
    When the pilot changes the view
    Then the view is chase

  Expectation: FPV looks out of the nose
    You see the picture from the camera in the nose of the plane. The camera points 20° up,
    as on a plane for FPV flight.
    Given the view is chase
    When the pilot changes the view
    Then the view is FPV

  Expectation: Line of sight is the view from the pilot box
    You see the plane from the point where you stand, as at the field. The sim starts in this
    view.
    Given the view is FPV
    When the pilot changes the view
    Then the view is line of sight

  Expectation: Auto-zoom off
    The zoom stays the same, as with your eyes. The plane becomes small when it flies away.
    Given auto-zoom is on
    When the pilot toggles auto-zoom
    Then auto-zoom is off

  Expectation: Auto-zoom on
    Given auto-zoom is off
    When the pilot toggles auto-zoom
    Then auto-zoom is on
